# Lighthouse temp user-data-dirs. When the lighthouse CLI runs on Linux/macOS
# but the underlying Chromium was built with a Windows-style temp path
# resolver, it creates a directory literally named
#   C:\Users\<user>\AppData\Local\lighthouse.<NNNNNN>\
# (yes, with backslashes in the directory name) inside whatever the cwd
# is at launch time. Without this rule, every `scripts/lighthouse-pwa.sh`
# run litters the repo with ~16 MB Chromium profile dirs and `git status`
# shows them.
#
# IMPORTANT: backslashes in `.gitignore` are escape characters. To match
# a literal backslash in a filename, double it in the pattern. The pattern
# below matches the literal directory name; the leading wildcard covers
# the random numeric suffix Lighthouse appends.
#
# Delete existing junk manually:
#   find . -maxdepth 1 -type d -name 'C:*' -exec rm -rf {} +
C:\\Users\\*\\AppData\\Local\\lighthouse.*

docs/**/*.jsonl